Bug 2056286 - Fix disabled Mark and Tag menu bar items in synthetic views. r=tobyp

InitMessageMenu used tab.folder (gFolder) to determine whether markMenu
and tagMenu should be enabled. For synthetic views (gloda search results,
conversation tabs) gFolder is not set, so the menus were incorrectly
disabled even though the displayed messages have real underlying folders.

Fix by using message?.folder (the message's real folder) with a fallback
to gFolder when no message is selected. This correctly enables mark and
tag menus for synthetic views while keeping them disabled for truly
folderless contexts (external messages, server roots). As a side effect,
markMenu is now also enabled in the standalone message window for
messages with a real folder, where it was previously always disabled;
this makes it consistent with the move and tag menus there.

Add synthetic view and message window tests to browser_messageMenu.js,
matching the existing coverage in browser_mailContext.js.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316116


